0..54 Comment "// This source models globular cells at dimension one."
55..57 Comment "//"
58..134 Comment "// `Glob` has an associator cell. A stated law does not orient. A stated law"
135..209 Comment "// has no default component. The Path reading supplies the associator from"
210..229 Comment "// `std.math.path`."
230..232 Comment "//"
233..309 Comment "// `PathCells` proves the right unit by conversion. It proves the associator"
310..389 Comment "// with the path theorem. `Discharged` omits the associator because `Path.here`"
390..428 Comment "// fills the converting path nestings."
429..431 Comment "//"
432..514 Comment "// - see: `pathological/higher-cells/path-cells.gandr` — a model of the naturals"
515..575 Comment "//   leaving the cell out, and a scope breaking a stated law"
576..650 Comment "// - see: `cat-shape.gandr` — the same theory with its associator a rule"
652..701 Comment "// `assoc` is the associator of path composition."
